## 6. RESPONSE PROTOCOLS

### 6.1 Immediate Actions Upon CSAE Detection

| Severity | Detection Method | Response |
|----------|-----------------|----------|
| **Critical** (Confirmed CSAM) | Automated hash match OR user report with evidence | Immediate account suspension + Content removal + NCMEC/Cybertip reporting within 24 hours |
| **High** (Suspected grooming) | Behavioral detection OR pattern analysis | Account restriction + Human review within 12 hours + Possible reporting |
| **Moderate** (Concerning behavior) | User report without evidence | Investigation + Warning if warranted |
| **Low** (Policy violations) | Automated flagging | Content removal + User notification |

### 6.2 Law Enforcement Cooperation

When cooperates fully with:
- **NCMEC (National Center for Missing & Exploited Children)** – Mandatory reporting for US-based incidents
- **International Authorities** – INTERPOL and local law enforcement referrals
- **Cybertipline** – Direct reporting of confirmed CSAM

**Response Commitment:**
- Preserve all relevant evidence (logs, content, metadata)
- Respond to legal requests within 24-48 hours
- Designated legal contact for law enforcement: [legal@when.app]

